<body>
<div type="edition" xml:lang="kan-Latn" rendition="class:kannada maturity:83215">
    
<p>
    <lb n="1"/>jēḍara dāsimayyaṁagaḷu dēvarige vastrava kuḍuva ṭāu <g ref="sym:doubleBar" type="punctuation">.</g>
    siriyāḷa-seṭṭi caṁgaḷavve dēvarige maganan ikkuva ṭāvu <g ref="sym:doubleBar" type="punctuation">.</g>
    kuṁbāṟa gu<supplied reason="omitted">ṁ</supplied>ḍana muṁde
    <lb n="2"/>baṁdhā<supplied reason="omitted">ṁd</supplied> <supplied reason="omitted">ā</supplied>ḍida naṁma śivanu <supplied reason="omitted"><g ref="sym:doubleBar" type="punctuation">.</g></supplied>

</p>
    </div>
    
    <div type="translation" source="bib:Desai1951-1952_02">
        <p>Here is <supplied reason="explanation">is depicted the scene of</supplied> Jēḍara <supplied reason="explanation">weaver</supplied> Dāsimayya offering cloth to the god <supplied reason="explanation">Śiva</supplied>.
            Here is depicted the scene of Siriyāḷa-seṭṭi and <supplied reason="explanation">his wife</supplied> Chaṁgaḷavve offering their son to the god <supplied reason="explanation">Śiva</supplied>.
            Our <supplied reason="explanation">god</supplied> Śiva came down and danced before Kuṁbāṟa <supplied reason="explanation">potter</supplied> Guṇḍa.
        </p>
       
    </div>
    
